SUMMARY:treyOS Milestone 1 shipped + cross-repo housekeeping
DESCRIPTION:Milestone 1 of treyOS (a new personal-operating-system proje
 ct) went from an empty repo to a working\, argue-with-able capacity mod
 el\, plus unrelated maintenance landed in three other repos the same d
 ay.\n\ntreyOS — Milestone 1 (Capacity Engine)\, all 7 issues closed:\n
 • Repo created (adaliaworks/treyOS)\, CLAUDE.md/SPEC.md committed\, 7
  GitHub milestones + 11 issues filed\n• #1 — Project scaffolding: R
 ails 8\, Postgres\, Solid Queue/Cache/Cable\, Kamal\, Standard Ruby\, C
 I\n• #2 — Domain schema & models: 9 tables (commitments\, commitmen
 t_events\, persons\, capacity_blocks\, ...)\, uuid primary keys\, Activ
 eRecord Encryption wired and verified against a live round trip\n•
 #3 — Manual commitment entry: CRUD + explicit state-transition method
 s\, each pairing a state change with an audit-trail event in the same
 transaction\n• #4 — Capacity engine core: a pure/DB-free CapacityEng
 ine computing floor/ceiling capacity and required load over a date ran
 ge\n• #5 — Backward pass & recovery-time warning: finds the next re
 al protected block (never hardcoded to a day of week)\, names the fewe
 st commitments that clear an overflow\n• #6 — Three-horizon dashboa
 rd: 0-14 day execution grid\, 15-90 day capacity-vs-load curve as a ser
 ver-rendered SVG\, 90-180 day monthly bands\n• #7 — Seed data & M1
 acceptance pass: a realistic synthetic quarter\, verified with a live
 browser walkthrough rather than just green tests\n\nFound and fixed re
 al bugs along the way rather than trusting the code: a validation that
  blocked capacity blocks from running to end-of-day\, a missing load-m
 ultiplier weighting in the backward pass that was silently hiding over
 flow\, an integer-division bug collapsing the chart's gridlines\, and
 a missing test-environment encryption keyset that would have broken CI
  on the first PR.\n\nOther repos (separate sessions\, same day):\n•
 facilitimer — #9 menu bar mini-mode implemented and closed\, completi
 ng Milestone 3\n• gevity-fit — repo cleanup: committed four previou
 sly local-only ICS worklogs\, added a .gitignore\n• app-gevity-fit
 — matching cleanup (PR #177\, open) plus two Dependabot merges: Rails
  8.1.3→8.1.3.1 (#166)\, Brakeman 8.0.5→8.0.6 (#175)\n\nRaw (un-round
 ed) window: treyOS session start ~2026-08-19T14:15Z (10:15 AM EDT\, es
 timated — substantial design discussion preceded the first commit)\,
  through the day's last confirmed deliverable\, the Brakeman Dependabo
 t merge at 2026-08-19T20:59:54Z (4:59:54 PM EDT). Rounded to 10:15–17
 :00 EDT.
END:VEVENT
